    "hardest_part": "Stringing together a clean, complete stage run: the scoring gates for Stages 2-5 require verified native finishes of all preceding stages, so I must finish Stages 1-5 in sequence, and sustaining car control on narrow, twisty top-down tracks for a full stage is very demanding.",
    "likely_failure": "Losing control and going off the road or hitting scenery, then having the car stuck or facing the wrong way with no manual recovery available; also blind corners where the 1-second action granularity causes oversteering into an obstacle, killing the run and forfeiting the finish bonus needed to progress.",
    "helpful_mechanics": "Automatic transmission removes shifting burden; automatic recovery exists if I get stuck; partial progress still awards verified segments, so even short clean stretches of Stage 1 score points; braking and handbrake allow careful low-speed navigation; Enter-based result navigation is straightforward.",
    "harmful_mechanics": "One-second discrete inputs make fine steering correction impossible and encourage overshoot; top-down view limits look-ahead to upcoming corners; no pause, manual restart or manual recovery, so a crash costs the whole attempt; the milestone structure heavily rewards full-stage finishes, which are exactly the hardest thing to achieve with coarse controls."
